ZERO OS 0.8.1 NATIVE FULLHD VERIFICATION
Date: 2026-11-16 UTC

FINAL TESTED ISO
SHA256:8d494eca3adbf8998b1674d4d7c4cd03308f40ba87ee3213a806fefa6c9f7d31
Bytes:17645568. This exact ISO remained unchanged throughout all final runs.

FOUR FULLHD BOOT MODES
BIOS x86-64: PASS,1920x1080,41 recorded actions.
BIOS x86-32 (-lm,-pae): PASS,1920x1080,41 recorded actions.
UEFI x86-64: PASS,1920x1080,41 recorded actions.
UEFI x86-32 (-lm): PASS,1920x1080,41 recorded actions.
All use QEMU TCG and standard VGA with32MiB video memory and1920x1080 EDID.
The BIOS handoff independently reports kind2,width1920,height1080,
stride1920,BGR format1. Every native QEMU screendump has1920x1080 pixels.
PNG conversion preserves dimensions; no host image resizing is performed.

The underlying framebuffer addresses individual native pixels: in each
mode, pixel1919,1079 becomes RGB(1,2,3) while its neighboring pixel does not.
Coordinatex1920 is rejected, and a subsequent layout redraw restores the
corner. This verifies a real1920-wide framebuffer rather than an enlarged
800/960-wide screenshot. The UI itself deliberately draws its original font,
frames and spacing at2x scale, with16x32 terminal cells. Every2x2 UI pixel
block was checked for consistency before the native single-pixel probe.

WINDOW INTERACTION
Actual emulated PS/2 F1..F5 keystrokes create/close/reuse a third window,
change focus and toggle tile/scroll layouts. Two incomplete write commands
survive F3/F4 switches and execute correctly on explicit Enter. Per-window
rootsA/B remain usable. Basic relative and absolute-path reads return the
known ext4 welcome file from a private32MiB copied fixture.
Clearing window2 preserves window1's complete976x640 text region exactly;
the cleared window's720x224 body changes as expected. No disk writes are
issued, and full hashes of all private ZeroFS/ext4 copies remain unchanged.

PIXEL GEOMETRY AND VISUAL REVIEW
check-screens.py independently verifies all four modes' complete2-pixel
window borders, tile gaps, focused scroll-frame borders, visible neighboring
borders and empty inter-window gaps. No text or drawing spills into gaps.
Native three-tile rectangles are(32,160,1040,800),
(1104,160,784,384),(1104,576,784,384).
The scroll focus is(512,160,896,800), with neighbors clipped at screen edges.
Actual images were visually inspected; an independent renderer review also
confirmed legible text, correct spacing and clean clipping in BIOS64's
initial two-window, three-tile and scrolling screenshots.
Animation was disabled to make caret/image equality checks deterministic.

LOW-VIDEO-MEMORY FALLBACK
BIOS x86-64: PASS,800x600,8 recorded actions.
UEFI x86-64: PASS,800x600,8 recorded actions.
Both use2MiB VGA memory,800x600 EDID and xmax800/ymax600, preventing FullHD.
Each boots the same final ISO, creates a third window and successfully
switches between tile and scroll layouts. No data disks are attached.
Fallback screenshots retain native800x600 dimensions.

EVIDENCE AND LIMITS
All six final VM processes exited; original user disks were never attached.
Native VirtualBox and physical hardware were not tested. QEMU and Python
scripts are external verification infrastructure, not guest implementation.
Best actual FullHD image:bios64/desktop-tiles.png.
Each boot mode retains desktop-tiles.png,desktop-scroll.png,initial view,
clear/pixel checks,serial output,actions.jsonl and a passing result.json.
screen-geometry.json records the independent border/gap oracle results.

Earlier fixture-* directories and probe-fixtures.py used the immutable old
0.8.0 ISO solely to inspect emulated VGA/firmware availability; they are not
0.8.1 feature evidence and are excluded from the delivery package.
Private disks,PPM snapshots,memory dumps,vars.fd and sockets are test-only
artifacts. Distribute scripts,JSON/text/serial logs and native PNGs; the
only delivered disk image remains the genuine bootable ISO.
